logement . type:
  description: |
    This information affects, in particular, the building’s footprint, but also the options for insulation work, for example.

    &gt; If you live in an unconventional home, such as a campervan, that’s no problem: select ‘flat’ and enter the square metres of what is, after all, your home.
  note: OCSTAT
logement . construction . empreinte amortie:
  formule: 696 kgCO2e / 60 m2
  note: Fribourg University Report 2021 (60-year depreciation period)
logement . construction . base . amortissement:
  formule:
    variations:
      - si: rénovation . travaux . travaux réalisés
        alors: 75
      - sinon: 60
  note: |
    SIA standard assumption
logement . habitants:
  par défaut: 2.1
  note: OCSTAT
logement . électricité . réseau . consommation estimée via le coût . saisie:
  unité: CHF/mois
logement . électricité . réseau . consommation:
  description: |
    Tip: You can find your annual electricity consumption on your bills or via your online account on the SIG website.

    &gt; If you live in more than one property (for example, if you have a second home), try to ‘consolidate’ these consumption figures into those for your main home to ensure the estimate is as accurate as possible.
logement . climatisation . nombre par défaut:
  formule: 0
logement . chauffage . fioul:
  titre: Heating oil
logement . chauffage:
  description: |
    &gt; This question covers all the energy sources you use to power your heating, water heater, hobs, etc.

    Some homes use only electricity, others are heated entirely by gas, and, less commonly, by wood or fuel oil.
    In other cases, a home may be heated mainly by electric heaters or a heat pump,
    but with wood as a supplementary source, for example. Finally, you can also include your gas consumption for your van or motorhome.

    Tick all the methods you use.
logement . chauffage . gaz . consommation précise:
  par défaut: parc français . CEREN . chauffage . consommation gaz par m2 * surface
  description: |
    Tip: You can find your annual energy consumption on your gas bills.

    &gt; For heating, your property management company may not provide you with your home’s consumption in kWh if you have a central heating boiler. You can enter the amount of your bill in CHF to estimate your kWh usage. If you have two bills – one for cooking gas and one for heating gas (service charges) – add the two amounts together.
logement . chauffage . gaz . consommation estimée via le coût . saisie:
  unité: CHF/mois
logement . chauffage . gaz . consommation estimée via le coût . facteur:
  unité: CHF/kWh
  formule: 0.143
  note: FSO average energy prices su-f-05.02.91, 2022 average - https://www.bfs.admin.ch/bfs/fr/home/statistiques/prix/indice-prix-consommation/resultats-detailles.assetdetail.25245904.html
logement . chauffage . gaz . intensité carbone:
  valeur: 0.23
  note: KBOB
logement . chauffage . fioul . consommation précise:
  question: What is your household’s annual heating oil consumption?
  description: |
    Tip: You can find your annual energy consumption on your heating oil bill or on the annual service charge statement sent by your property management company.
logement . chauffage . gaz . intensité carbone gaz utilisateur:
  formule: gaz . intensité carbone
logement . chauffage . réseau de chaleur . consommation précise:
  aide: null
  description: |
    The carbon content per kWh of heat supplied by a district heating network depends heavily on the network to which you are connected.

    Tip: You can find your annual energy consumption on your bills or in your online account on your supplier’s website.

    &gt; Your property management company may not provide you with your home’s consumption in kWh if the boiler is centrally located. You can enter your bill amount in CHF to estimate your kWh consumption.
services sociétaux:
  formule:
    somme:
      - services publics
  description: |
    This post includes the footprint of Swiss public services.
  note: Regional carbon footprints of the City of Geneva and the Canton of Geneva
services sociétaux . services publics:
  formule: 1583
  note: calculation based on the VdG and Canton territorial carbon footprints (see ‘societal services’ file)
logement . propriétaire:
  description: |
    As a tenant, it is obviously difficult to make the investments needed to improve the property’s environmental footprint: insulating your home or switching to a different energy source are measures that only landlords can carry out. That doesn’t stop tenants from asking them to do so!
  par défaut: non
